
This is a very well commented chunk of code that implements the
Chudnovsky algorithm which you can read about here : 

    https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chudnovsky_algorithm

You may also, if you are brave, read a detailed proof here :

    https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.00533

For fun and happy happy joy joy feelings feel free to run this
chud with 2048 bits of precision and 16 loops to get a value 
estimate of pi that is correct to 226 digits after the decimal
point.  Just do ./chud 2048 16 and watch.

Expect some clean up and a better readme real soon now, 

    Dennis Clarke 


ps: At some point I may re-write this thing to automagically
    adjust internal precision for all computations in order
    to get a better result. Maybe.  See Pollard Rho code for
    and example of this sort of precision adjustment stuff.


NOTE: a snazzy implementation can be seen in marian_check_pi.c
      where we get the bit precision automagically revised in
      a while loop.  I DID NOT WRITE THAT and YES IT WORKS!

